## The Calling of Saint Matthew: a holy story in a tax office
sources:
    - id: wiki
      title: The Calling of Saint Matthew
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2026
      finding: 1599–1600 for the Contarelli Chapel, San Luigi dei Francesi; Matthew 9:9, the call at the tax booth; the bearded man usually read as Matthew pointing at himself
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Calling_of_Saint_Matthew
    - id: angel
      title: Saint Matthew and the Angel
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2026
      finding: 'The first altarpiece (1602) was rejected: Matthew looked like a peasant, poorly groomed, with dirty feet; destroyed in Berlin in 1945'
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Matthew_and_the_Angel
    - id: cara
      title: Caravaggio
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2026
      finding: Born 1571; worked directly from live models; the Contarelli side paintings were an immediate sensation in 1600
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caravaggio

    card title "The Calling of Saint Matthew"

    image art cites ["wiki","angel","cara"] credit "Caravaggio, 1599–1600. Contarelli Chapel, San Luigi dei Francesi, Rome. Public domain." x 500 y 334 width 690 url https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Michelangelo_Caravaggio_040.jpg/1920px-Michelangelo_Caravaggio_040.jpg look screen regions.bare_feet [0.8,0.82,0.2,0.16] regions.bearded [0.276,0.41,0.104,0.16] regions.bearded_hand [0.307,0.53,0.07,0.035] regions.boy_feather [0.4,0.4,0.15,0.18] regions.call_line [0.26,0.33,0.66,0.26] regions.coin_counter [0.19,0.49,0.09,0.17] regions.coins [0.255,0.65,0.045,0.025] regions.counting [0.19,0.49,0.12,0.19] regions.dark_wall [0,0,0.48,0.4] regions.holy_pair [0.72,0.33,0.28,0.67] regions.jesus [0.64,0.33,0.36,0.14] regions.jesus_face [0.855,0.355,0.05,0.06] regions.jesus_hand [0.64,0.395,0.075,0.045] regions.old_man [0.17,0.4,0.1,0.12] regions.peter [0.75,0.36,0.23,0.61] regions.room [0,0,0.81,0.4] regions.sword [0.415,0.7,0.17,0.24] regions.swordsman [0.47,0.45,0.18,0.48] regions.swordsman_all [0.415,0.45,0.235,0.49] regions.table [0.06,0.4,0.6,0.35] regions.window [0.5,0,0.31,0.335]

This is Caravaggio's Calling of Saint Matthew, painted for a church in Rome in 1600 — an (@highlight art:table strength soft@)d it looks like a tax office.

So why would anyone set a holy story (@highlight art:counting lift true@) in a room where money gets counted?

Caravaggio was not yet thirty, and he painted straight from live models, people he could find in Rome.
    portrait caravaggio of Caravaggio cameo true

    erase caravaggio

The story is from the Gospel:  (@highlight art:jesus lift true@)Jesus sees a tax collector, Matthew, at his booth, and says, follow me.

Start with the room: (@highlight art:room strength soft lift true@) a bare wall, a shuttered window, a plain table. No temple, no columns, no angels.

    camera on ["art@[0.12,0.38,0.32,0.32]"]

On the table lie a few coins, and a young man counts them with his head down.
    highlight art:coins art:coin_counter

An old man in spectacles leans over him, checking the sums.
    highlight art:old_man lift true

    camera reset true

It is a counting room any Roman of the day would know: money in, money out.
    highlight art:table lift true

    camera on ["art@[0.36,0.38,0.32,0.6]"]

Then the clothes. A boy in a feathered cap and a bright, slashed doublet.
    highlight art:boy_feather lift true

Beside him, a yo (@highlight art:swordsman_all lift true@)ung man with puffed sleeves and a sword at his hip: street fashion of 1600, not of the Bible.

    camera reset true

    ask "Tap one of the two who belong to another time." spot holy_pair on art
        intro: Most of these men could have walked in from a Roman street. Two could not.
        right: Yes: Jesus and Peter, who have stepped in from the Bible.
        wrong: Look for long robes and bare feet, on the right.

    highlight art:holy_pair lift true duration 2

    camera on ["art@[0.62,0.3,0.38,0.7]"]

Jesus and Peter wear plain, timeless robes (@highlight art:bare_feet strength strong rest grey lift true@), and Peter's feet are bare: the way painters had long dressed Bible figures.

    camera reset true

So the painting holds two times at once: the Bible's on the right, Caravaggio's own at the table.
    highlight art:holy_pair art:table

And Jesus reaches a (@highlight art:call_line strength soft lift true@)cross from one into the other, as if the call could come into any room, today.

    camera on ["art:table"]

Matthew, most think, is the bearded man, pointing at himself as if to ask: me?
    highlight art:bearded lift true

An apostle as an ordinary man at a  (@highlight art:table lift true@)money table, among coins and fashionable young men: for a church, that was a risk.

    camera reset true

Two years later, the same church turned down his first altarpiece of Matthew (@highlight art:bare_feet strength soft lift true@): the saint looked like a peasant with dirty feet.

He had to paint it again. Yet thes (@highlight art:call_line strength soft lift true@)e side paintings made him famous almost overnight.

Bruegel had pushed a myth into the corner of a working day. Caravaggio brings the holy story right into the working room.
    highlight art:table art:jesus strength soft

    camera on ["art:call_line"]

The daring idea: holiness needs no special place. It can walk into a tax office, among people dressed like you.
    highlight art:call_line rest paper lift true

    camera reset true

    quiz "A film-maker retells the Good Samaritan the way Caravaggio might. Which choice follows him?"
        right: Today's clothes and street: the people of the story look like the people watching, just as Matthew's companions looked like Romans of 1600.
        wrong: Whose clothes do his tax collectors wear: the Bible's, or his viewers'?
        * Robes on a desert road
        * Modern street, old robes
        + Today's clothes and street

Four hundred years on, the coins are still on the table, and the call still comes into an ordinary room.
    highlight art:coins art:call_line strength soft

